    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Quillsen is delighted to present this attractive semi-detached family home to the market. Situated within a mature and highly sought-after residential neighbourhood, No. 4 Windsor Park enjoys a highly convenient location close to the excellent amenities, schools, recreational facilities and transport links that Monkstown and the surrounding area have to offer.\n\nSet on a generous site with an attached garage, ample off-street parking and a beautifully established rear garden, the property offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation together with excellent scope for modernisation and extension, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises an entrance hall, a spacious living room, an inter-connecting dining room overlooking the rear garden, and a generously proportioned kitchen/breakfast room. In addition there is a utility room and a shower room downstairs. Upstairs, off a bright landing area, there are three well-appointed bedrooms, and a family bathroom.\n\nA particular feature of the property is the mature rear garden, which enjoys a high degree of privacy and is bordered by a rich variety of established trees, shrubs and planting. Predominantly laid in lawn, it provides an ideal setting for family life, outdoor entertaining and gardening enthusiasts alike, while also offering excellent potential to further enhance the accommodation, subject to planning permission.\n\nThe location offers exceptional convenience, with Monkstown Village within easy reach and a superb selection of cafés, restaurants, boutiques and local amenities nearby. Blackrock and Dún Laoghaire are also close at hand, providing an extensive choice of shopping, leisure and coastal amenities. Recreational facilities in the area include Monkstown Lawn Tennis Club, Monkstown DLR Pool & Fitness Centre, Seapoint and the many scenic walks along Dublin Bay.\n\nThe area is particularly popular with families due to the excellent choice of highly regarded primary and secondary schools nearby. Transport links are equally impressive, with Salthill & Monkstown DART Station, numerous Dublin Bus routes and the Aircoach all within easy reach, providing convenient access to the city centre, surrounding suburbs and Dublin Airport.\n\nCombining spacious accommodation, a mature private garden, an attached garage and a highly convenient Monkstown location, this is an excellent opportunity to acquire a family home with tremendous potential in a well-established residential neighbourhood."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor\n\nEntrance Porch\nDoor to hallway.\n\nEntrance Hallway - 4.3m (14'1\") x 2.2m (7'3\")\nUnderstairs storage. Ceiling coving and rose.\n\nLiving Room - 3.9m (12'10\") x 3.77m (12'4\")\nTiled fireplace, ceiling coving and rose. Attractive folding doors to dining room.\n\nDining Room - 4m (13'1\") x 3.6m (11'10\")\nCeiling coving and rose. Double glazed patio doors to magnificent rear garden.\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room - 3m (9'10\") x 5.2m (17'1\")\nAmple wall and floor units. Stainless steel sink unit. Plumbed for washing machine and dishwasher. Recessed lighting, door to utility room and door to garage.\n\nUtility Room - 1.47m (4'10\") x 2.1m (6'11\")\nTiled floor. Door to shower room.\n\nShower Room - 1.3m (4'3\") x 2.1m (6'11\")\nTiled shower, pedestal whb and wc. Fully tiled.\n\nGarage - 4.8m (15'9\") x 2.57m (8'5\")\nDoor to kitchen/breakfast room.\n\nFirst Floor\n\nLanding\nCupboard with gas boiler. Stira stairs to a spacious partly floored attic.\n\nFront Bedroom 1 - 3.9m (12'10\") x 3.56m (11'8\")\nExtensive built in wardrobes and vanity unit.\n\nRear Bedroom 2 - 4m (13'1\") x 3.42m (11'3\")\nBuilt in wardrobe and vanity unit.\n\nFront Bedroom 3 - 2.5m (8'2\") x 2.41m (7'11\")\nBuilt in wardrobe and vanity unit.\n\nBathroom - 1.77m (5'10\") x 2.55m (8'4\")\nBath with telephone shower, pedestal whb and wc. Fully tiled.\n\nOutside\nVery large front garden with parking for 4-5 cars. Mature trees and shrubs. There is a good sized garage.\n\nAn exceptionally large sunny north west facing and secluded rear garden incorporating a variety of mature trees and shrubs. Garden shed.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
